# test/sessions/ — transcripts that convicted a defect.
#
# Each file here is evidence, not an assertion: the session as it was
# recorded, kept under the F-number of the defect it exposed, so the
# fixme.md citation resolves and the next investigator replays the
# original rather than reconstructing it from a description.  A
# replay is EXPECTED to diff once the defect is fixed — the diff is
# the point.  New friends arrive named `F<number>-<what-happened>.ges`.
#
# F110: the zoom wedged.  This transcript shows the model's mirror
# answering "smaller" twelve times on a NINE-rung ladder while the
# window sat at the largest — the fact that broke the case open
# (recorded 2026-08-13; root cause and fix in fixme.md F110).
#
# A gestate editor session — replay it with
#
#     python -m gestate.sessionlog <this file>
#
#: editing /home/cheery/gestate/hello.ges
#
# Each line is a command and what it answered.  The
# answers are the diff: a replay that says something
# else is the report.

